# HATC i18n

- All copy lives in JSON message files under `src/messages/` (`zh-Hant`, `zh-Hans`, `en`).
  `zh-Hant` is the default locale.
- Never hard-code user-facing text in components; always read from messages.
- Reuse keys: identical text must NOT get a new key. Search existing keys first and
  reuse. Only add a key when the string is genuinely new.
- Keep the same key set across all locales; do not let files drift out of sync.
- Use clear, hierarchical keys (e.g. `home.hero.title`), not the literal text as the key.
- Operational links (customer service, contact) come from CMS config, not messages.

## Example

```json
// ❌ BAD: duplicate keys for the same text
{ "home.cta": "聯絡我們", "footer.contactUs": "聯絡我們" }

// ✅ GOOD: one shared key, reused in both places
{ "common.contactUs": "聯絡我們" }
```

## CMS content locales (第七十一輪, 2026-10-14)

`zh-Hant` is the canonical locale for CMS content too, not just for messages, and
`localization.fallback: true` only lets the **other** locales fall back to it — the
canonical locale has nothing to fall back to.

- **A required localized field left empty in `zh-Hant` removes the document from
  every locale**, because the readers drop a document whose title is empty in the
  requested locale (`mapSummary` in `src/lib/announcements.ts` /
  `src/lib/academyArticles.ts`) and the other locales resolve to the empty
  `zh-Hant` value. It also used to remove it from `sitemap.xml` in every locale;
  the sitemap now enumerates per locale, but the page still 404s where the title
  is missing. Seven production announcements were invisible this way.
- **Author in `zh-Hant` first, then press 一鍵機器翻譯.** The button no longer
  requires it (it translates from whichever locale is most complete, ties going to
  `zh-Hant`), but the canonical locale is the one the owner proofreads and the one
  every fallback resolves to.
- **Never paste the same text into all three locales.** Payload only falls back
  when a locale is *empty*, so three identical values mean the English site really
  does display Chinese — strictly worse than leaving the other two empty
  (第六十九輪, `funding-methods`).
- A missing-title gap is surfaced in `/admin` above each collection's list table
  (`src/components/payload/LocaleCoverageNotice.tsx`); batch backfill via
  `scripts/translate-content.ts` (DEPLOYMENT §4.2). Machine output is a draft.
- 🚩 **"It shows up in `/admin`" does not mean that locale has content.** Payload's
  admin list query honours `localization.fallback: true`, so an empty `zh-Hant`
  title is displayed as the `zh-Hans` one and the back office looks healthy while
  the public site drops the document. Check coverage with
  `?locale=<l>&fallback-locale=null` against the REST API, or read the notice panel
  (it queries with `fallbackLocale: false`). A CLI backfill does not revalidate —
  press Save once in `/admin` afterwards or the public pages stay stale.
